    "findings": [
      "Directly read all eleven boards, including the earlier four boards and remaining boards five through eleven. The structure-capture and repeated-measurement plates have visible projected top and side faces; their orange blocks are explicitly labelled role-only rather than a GPU measurement.",
      "The independent six-sample example retains values 8, 10, 9, 11, 8, 10 ms and mean 9.33 ms with range 8–11 ms. Teal bars rise above their projected base across the sampled progression, and fictional/example and actual-condition qualifications remain readable.",
      "Observed the exact old/new boundaries 760/761, 1564/1565 and 2493/2494. The observation-versus-implementation scene uses separate orange and teal projected platforms, grey blocks and growing yellow arrows without treating an image alone as implementation or performance proof.",
      "The conclusion begins at frame 2494 and retains six projected blocks labelled brightness number, bake, realtime shadows, screen/grid, ray/cache and reconstruction. Orange links progressively connect them, with readable qualifications that techniques coexist and a year alone does not establish every game's implementation.",
      "The final sampled frame 3426 remains populated. Black background, white text, yellow headings and role colours are readable in these clean source samples. Final burned captions, continuous moving playback, final mix and final footage composition remain separate pending checks."
